<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>How to Play</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: linear-gradient(#FFFFFF, #cfe2f3);
        }

        .navbar {
            background-color: #cfe2f3;
            padding: 12px 20px;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: space-between;
            background: linear-gradient(#B0D0ED, #cfe2f3);
        }

        .navbar-left {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 12px;
        }
      
        .navbar-right {
            display: flex;
            gap: 10px;
        }

        .logo-box {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            padding: 0;
        }

        .logo-img {
            height: 44px;
            width: auto;
            display: block;
        }

        .site-name {
            color: #1a5276;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 16px;
        }

        .navbar a {
            color: black;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .navbar a:hover {
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        .main {
            padding: 30px 40px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 3em;
            color: black;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        h3 {
            text-align: center;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 1em;
            color: black;
            margin-top: 10px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .section-title {
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 1.5em;
            text-align: center;
            color: black;
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        .content-box {
            border: 1px solid #1a5276;
            border-radius: 15px;
            background-color: white;
            min-height: 100px;
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            font-size: 20px;
            color: #333;
            text-align: center;
        }
      
        .columns {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            gap: 20px;
        }

        .column {
            flex: 1;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <div class="navbar">
        <div class="navbar-left">
            <div class="logo-box">
                <svg class="logo-img" viewBox="0 0 1140 1140" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Game Night logo" role="img">
                    <circle cx="570" cy="570" r="520" fill="none" stroke="#097969" stroke-width="40"/>
                    <path fill="#097969" fill-rule="evenodd"
                          d="M 570 180 C 410 180 300 320 300 500 C 275 680 215 820 240 920 Q 320 965 410 935 Q 475 975 540 925 Q 610 970 675 915 Q 740 960 810 900 C 825 750 840 600 840 500 C 840 320 730 180 570 180 Z M 570 230 C 425 230 350 340 350 510 C 330 680 285 800 295 900 Q 365 940 440 915 Q 500 945 555 910 Q 615 940 670 910 Q 720 930 760 905 C 775 750 790 600 790 510 C 790 340 715 230 570 230 Z"/>
                    <circle cx="500" cy="480" r="30" fill="#097969"/>
                    <circle cx="640" cy="480" r="30" fill="#097969"/>
                    <ellipse cx="570" cy="580" rx="30" ry="42" fill="#097969"/>
                </svg>
            </div>
            <span class="site-name">Quinstance</span>
        </div>
        <div class="navbar-right">
            <a href="/home">Home</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <main class="main">
        <h1>How to Play!</h1>
      
        <div class="columns">
            <div class="column">
                <div class="content-box">
                    <h2 class="section-title">Quizzes</h2>
                    <h3>Create a Quiz</h3>
                    <p>Create quizzes with questions that have up to 4 possible answers - but only one correct option!
                    Quizzes have an assigned Category and Key Stage, with a wide range of options to choose from.</p>
                    <h3>Edit Quizzes</h3>
                    <p>Edit anything you customised! Thought of a new name for your Quiz? Think a question is too easy
                    or way too difficult? Edit that too - no need to recreate a quiz or question!</p>
                    <h3>Host a Quiz</h3>
                    Hosting your quiz has never been easier. Just create a lobby and customise how you want students to play,
                    then share the randomly generated code given and press 'Start'! However, lobbies must contain at least
                    one player to start, and two players for minigames to be enabled.
                    <h3>Delete a Quiz</h3>
                    <p>Not happy with your quiz? Not to worry! You can just delete it and try again.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="column">
                <div class="content-box">
                    <h2 class="section-title">Minigames</h2>
                    <p>We have four minigames on offer. If minigames aren't your style, they can be toggled on/off in the
                    lobby setup and settings page offered during quiz hosting. Each minigame has an equal chance to
                    appear after a question, if at least two people got it wrong!
                    <h3>Maths</h3>
                    <p>Solve as many simple maths problems as you can in the given time. The player(s) with the least score
                    will become a ghost! Watch out - if you answer a maths question wrong, you will be stunned for 3 seconds,
                    so make sure you're quick and accurate!
                    <h3>Potions</h3>
                    <p>A simple game of luck. Pick a potion and hope that the one you picked wasn't the "ghost" potion. All players
                    who picked the ghost potion will become a ghost!
                    <h3>Rooms</h3>
                    <p>Players will have the option to pick a door, with three on offer. If all players pick the same door,
                    everyone is safe. Otherwise, the door with the most players will have a ghost hiding in it, turning those
                    players into ghosts!
                    <h3>Words</h3>
                    <p>A 5x5 grid with letters is generated and requires players to create the longest word they can think of
                    from those given letters. If the letters they use aren't in the grid or the word isn't real, they will have
                    to try again - no cheating! The player(s) with the shortest word in the lobby become ghosts!
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="column">
                <div class="content-box">
                    <h2 class="section-title">Becoming a Ghost:</h2>
                    <p>It's not game over if you become a ghost - minigames enabled or not, if a ghost player gets a
                    question right, they are revived and become a normal player again!</p>
                    <br>
                    <p>When a player becomes a ghost, they are unable to score points until they are revived. Ghost players
                    can still take part in quizzes and minigames.
                    <h3>With Minigames Enabled</h3>
                    <p>If a player loses a Minigame, they will become a ghost. If a lobby only has one non-ghost player,
                    if the remaining player gets a question wrong, they will automatically become a ghost!</p>
                    <h3>No Minigames Enabled</h3>
                    <p>If the host has no minigames enabled and a player gets a question wrong, they will become a ghost!
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

</body>
</html>
